  "sport": "basketball",
  "title": "Pass and go to the basket",
  "description": "Two lines: one at the top outside the three-point line, everyone with a ball, and one on the wing. The first player at the top passes to the wing. Straight after the pass the passer makes a jab step – a short step away from the basket – and then cuts hard to the basket in front of an imagined defender. The wing player hits the cutter in stride and the cutter finishes with a lay-up.\n\nRotation: the shooter takes their own rebound and joins the back of the wing line. The wing player runs to the top line. Run it from both sides so players finish with both the right and left hand.\n\nProgression: put a passive defender on the passer who turns their head to watch the ball when the pass is made.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Pass and go right away – don't stand and admire the pass."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The jab sells the cut: one short, sharp step away, then explode to the basket."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Cut in front of the defender and show a clear target hand."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "The wing passes to where the cutter is going, not where they are."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
